<title>USA: Seagram's Geffen records trim staff.</title>
<headline>Seagram's Geffen records trim staff.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seagram Co Ltd's Geffen Records said it cut 20 positions from a 205-member workforce.</p>
<p>&quot;We recognize that in order to stay competitive and ensure future growth companies have to change - Geffen Records has already re-invented itself several times over the years,&quot; the company said in a release.</p>
<p>The job cuts came at the end of last week. &quot;To best take advantage of the evolving marketplace, we've made the very difficult decision to re-direct our resources by eliminating 20 staff positions spread throughout the company on all levels,&quot; it said. A spokeswoman said the decision came as a result of overhead and revenue concerns.</p>
</text>
